SUMMARY:Mocktails & Meaning™: Peace-Building Between Israelis and Palestinians
DESCRIPTION:On December 17th\, we’ll welcome Rabbi Jack Paskoff of Congregation Shaarai Shomayim for a thoughtful conversation about Israel\, Palestine\, peacebuilding\, and human rights. \nDrawing from his experiences visiting Israel five times since the war began on October 7\, 2023\, Rabbi Paskoff will share what he has learned through conversations with grassroots organizations bringing Israelis and Palestinians together for peacebuilding\, as well as Israeli human rights organizations. \nThis Mocktails & Meaning™ session will offer space to listen\, learn\, ask questions\, and engage in thoughtful conversation around a complex and deeply important topic.
URL:https://apostlesucc.org/event/mocktails-meaning-peace-building-between-israelis-and-palestinians/
LOCATION:Church of the Apostles UCC\, 1850 Marietta Ave\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17603\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://apostlesucc.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Mocktails-Meaning-Flyer-Banner-Landscape-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
